   chapter 13 (IPsec, IKE, IKEv2); the shapes: FD 2.35 and 2.36.

   Version 1: a row is an IKE proposal, an IKE policy, an IPsec proposal and
   a map, each on one line, and an access list for the map. A peer "any"
   makes a dynamic map.
   - On a tunnel interface (the style "tunnel_if") the list lets everything
     through, as the routes choose what goes into the tunnel, and the tunnel
     interface names the map (interfaces.j2). The names are made from the
     number of the tunnel interface.
   - Without one (the style "policy") the list is made from the selectors
     of the row, and the interface of the row names the map (interfaces.j2).
     A row that the LNS of L2TP names has no interface: the tunnel
     interfaces of the LNS name the map, in transport mode. The map has the
     name of the row, the other parts are numbered p1, p2 and so on.
